    <title>M1 PHOBOS SHAPE MODEL</title>
    <information_model_version>1.15.0.0</information_model_version>
    <product_class>Product_Observational</product_class>
    <Citation_Information>
      <author_list>Thomas, P.C.</author_list>
      <publication_year>2021</publication_year>
      <description>Numerical shape model of M1 Phobos, derived from Viking orbiter images with some
checks with Mariner 9 and Phobos 2 data.  The model has uncertainties of a few
hundred meters in places, especially between 35 and 190 degrees longitude.  This
shape model consists of a grid with points every 2 degrees in latitude and longitude,
with a radius in km associated with each point.  The model is written with both 0 and
360 longitude entries.  Coordinates are planetocentric.  Phobos rotates synchronously
with its orbital period, with libration of about 1 degree.  Spin pole: RA=317.68,
Dec= 52.90  J2000 in degrees. Prime meridian W = 35.06 + 1128.8445850d in degrees,
where d is the number of days from the standard epoch (JD 2451545.0).</description>
    </Citation_Information>
